.TH "XmParsePicture" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmParsePicture\fP,
\fB\%XmGetNewPictureState\fP,
\fB\%XmPictureProcessCharacter\fP,
\fB\%XmPictureDoAutoFill\fP,
\fB\%XmPictureGetCurrentString\fP,
\fB\%XmPictureDeleteState\fP,
\fB\%XmPictureDelete\fP \(em Functions that match text against a picture
.iX "XmParsePicture"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmParsePicture"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmGetNewPictureState"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmPictureProcessCharacter"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmPictureDoAutoFill"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmPictureGetCurrentString"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmPictureDeleteState"
.iX "Picture functions" "XmPictureDelete"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/Picture\&.h>
.PP
\fBXmPicture \fBXmParsePicture\fP\fR(
\fBchar *\fBinput\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmPictureDelete\fP\fR(
\fBXmPicture \fBpicture\fR\fR);
.PP
\fBXmPictureState \fBXmGetNewPictureState\fP\fR(
\fBXmPicture \fBpicture\fR\fR);
\fBchar *\fBXmPictureProcessCharacter\fP\fR(
\fBXmPictureState \fBstate\fR\fR,
\fBchar \fBin\fR\fR,
\fBBoolean *\fBis_finished\fR\fR);
\fBchar *\fBXmPictureDoAutoFill\fP\fR(
\fBXmPictureState \fBstate\fR\fR);
\fBchar *\fBXmPictureGetCurrentString\fP\fR(
\fBXmPictureState \fBstate\fR\fR);
\fBvoid \fBXmPictureDeleteState\fP\fR(
\fBXmPictureState \fBstate\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
A picture is a pattern that a string typed in a field must match, such
as \fB\%(###)###-####\fP for a telephone number; the DataField widget
checks its text against the picture of its \fB\%XmNpicture\fP resource
with
these functions\&.  The syntax of pictures is described in
\fB\%XmDataField\fP(3)\&.
.PP
\fB\%XmParsePicture\fP compiles the picture \fIinput\fP\&.
\fB\%XmPictureDelete\fP frees a compiled picture\&.
.PP
\fB\%XmGetNewPictureState\fP creates a matching state, at the start of
the
picture\&.  \fB\%XmPictureProcessCharacter\fP feeds the next character
of
the text to the state: the character is accepted if the picture
allows it at this point, after being made upper case if the picture
asks for an upper case letter\&.  \fB\%XmPictureGetCurrentString\fP
returns
the text accepted so far\&.  \fB\%XmPictureDoAutoFill\fP appends the
characters that the picture imposes at this point (literal
characters, such as the \fB\%-\fP of the telephone number) for as long
as
there is only one possibility\&.  \fB\%XmPictureDeleteState\fP frees a
state\&.
.IP "\fIinput\fP" 10
Specifies the picture\&.
.IP "\fIpicture\fP" 10
Specifies the compiled picture\&.
.IP "\fIstate\fP" 10
Specifies the matching state\&.
.IP "\fIin\fP" 10
Specifies the character\&.
.IP "\fIis_finished\fP" 10
Returns True if the text accepted so far matches the whole picture,
or if the character was rejected, and False otherwise\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
\fB\%XmParsePicture\fP returns the compiled picture, and
\fB\%XmGetNewPictureState\fP the state\&.
\fB\%XmPictureProcessCharacter\fP
returns a pointer to the accepted character within the current string,
or NULL if the character was rejected; a rejected character leaves
the state with no possible match, so the caller starts again from a
new state with the text it keeps\&.  \fB\%XmPictureDoAutoFill\fP and
\fB\%XmPictureGetCurrentString\fP return the current string\&.  The
strings
belong to the state\&.
.SH "BUGS"
.PP
The current string of a state has room for 1023 characters, and is
not checked: longer text must not be fed to a state\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmDataField\fP(3)\&.
